    "id": "ct_mcq_285",
    "type": "mcq",
    "topic_id": "integrated_challenge",
    "prerequisite_topics": ["math_alg_inequalities"],
    "marks": 1,
    "difficulty": 6,
    "paper": 2,
    "section": "B",
    "question_en": "A linear programming problem involves maximizing $P = 4x + 3y$. If the vertices of the feasible region are $(2, 2)$, $(6, 1)$, and $(3, 5)$, find the maximum value of $P$.",
    "question_zh": "一個線性規劃問題要求最大化 $P = 4x + 3y$。若可行解區域的頂點為 $(2, 2)$、$(6, 1)$ 及 $(3, 5)$，求 $P$ 的最大值。",
    "options": [
      "A. 14",
      "B. 25",
      "C. 27",
      "D. 30"
    ],
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "solution_steps_en": [
      "Substitute each vertex into $P = 4x + 3y$:",
      "$(2, 2) \\Rightarrow P = 4(2) + 3(2) = 8 + 6 = 14$.",
      "$(6, 1) \\Rightarrow P = 4(6) + 3(1) = 24 + 3 = 27$.",
      "$(3, 5) \\Rightarrow P = 4(3) + 3(5) = 12 + 15 = 27$.",
      "The maximum value is 27."
    ],
    "solution_steps_zh": [
      "將每個頂點代入 $P = 4x + 3y$：",
      "$(2, 2) \\Rightarrow P = 14$。",
      "$(6, 1) \\Rightarrow P = 27$。",
      "$(3, 5) \\Rightarrow P = 27$。",
      "最大值為 27。"
    ],
    "diagram_json": null,
    "tags": ["linear-programming", "optimization"],
    "status": "approved"
  },
  {
